
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# ── Title line (write it in the blank line above) ──────────────────────────
# type    feat | fix | perf | refactor | test | docs | build | ci | chore | revert
# scope   package or area of the main change: state, tui, gateway, run, turn,
#         memory, migrate, tool, process, assembly, llm, mcp, lsp, config,
#         session, skill, channel, frontend, npm, docs; for cross-area changes
#         pick the single most relevant one
# subject English imperative, whole line <= 100 characters, starts lowercase,
#         no trailing period
#   e.g.: fix(state): keep the exec timing triple whole for sub-ms tools
#
# Enable this template: git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# DCO sign-off: `git commit -s` appends "Signed-off-by: <user.name> <user.email>".
# With the repository hooks installed (`make hooks`), prepare-commit-msg adds
# the sign-off automatically and commit-msg checks the title.
#
# ── Body: one blank line after the title, wrap at <= 72 characters ─────────
# The three sections below are required; keep unused optional sections
# commented out.

Why:
# What the problem is and why it happens. For a bug fix, name the root cause,
# not the symptom, and never present "add a nil check / fallback / retry"
# as the cause.

What:
# List the changes as bullets: behavior changes, interface changes, dead code
# removed, renames.
# -

Verification:
# The commands actually run and their results; list nothing you did not run.
# - CGO_ENABLED=1 go test -tags fts5 ./... -count=1
# - go vet ./... (add GOOS=linux / GOOS=windows for platform-specific code)
# - deadcode ./...; no graph.json change after scripts/package-graph.sh
# - cd frontend && pnpm build (when touching the frontend)
# - On a real machine: TUI / web scenario + the observed result (required for
#   user-visible behavior changes)

# ── Optional sections: remove the leading # when needed ────────────────────
#
# Schema:
# - stateSchemaVersion N -> N+1, migration <func name>
# - how existing rows are migrated; which rows are dropped and why
# - sqlite_master matches a freshly created database after migration (<test name>)
#
# Refs: docs/plan/<PLAN_FILE>.md (<task id>)
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: <who is affected + how to migrate>
